-- title:
--   Fixed points of the diagonal automorphism of W[[x,y]]/(xy-π)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$, and assume $W$ is precomplete for the ideal $(\pi)$ and $\pi$-adically separated in the sense that an element divisible by $\pi^n$ for every $n$ is zero. Let $e$ be a nonzero natural number and let $\zeta, \zeta' \in W$ satisfy $\zeta^e = 1$ and $\zeta\zeta' = 1$, and assume $\zeta^m - 1$ is a non-zero-divisor in $W$ for every $m$ with $0 < m < e$. Write $R_\pi$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0, X_1]]$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \pi$, and $\mathrm{mk}$ for the quotient map. The assertion is that there exists a $W$-algebra automorphism $\delta$ of $R_\pi$ with two properties: first, $\delta(\mathrm{mk}\,F) = \mathrm{mk}(\mathrm{rescale}\,(\zeta,\zeta')\,F)$ for every $F \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$, where rescaling multiplies the coefficient of $X_0^{a}X_1^{b}$ by $\zeta^{a}\zeta'^{b}$; and second, for every $z \in R_\pi$ one has $\delta(z) = z$ if and only if $z = \mathrm{mk}\,F$ for some power series $F$ all of whose nonzero coefficients sit in multidegrees $(a,b)$ with $a \equiv b \pmod e$.
--
--   This identifies the $\mu_e$-fixed subring of the crossing model $W[[x,y]]/(xy-\pi)$, under the diagonal action $x \mapsto \zeta x$, $y \mapsto \zeta' y$, as the set of classes represented by series supported in weights divisible by $e$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_powMap_range_eq_fixedPoints`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_powMap_range_eq_fixedPoints), which matches this fixed subring with the image of the map $u \mapsto x^e$, $v \mapsto y^e$ from the crossing model for $\pi^e$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_diagAut_fixed_iff.lean

